ind":"update","title":"Demo Update: Inverted Y-Axis Support + Opening Puzzle Guidance","summary":"Thank you to everyone who has played The Wake Event demo and shared feedback through the Steam forums.This update adds:An Invert Vertical Look option for mouse and controller.The setting is available from both the Main Menu and Pause Menu.A fix for terminals briefly reopening during a successful puzzle sequence.Additional stability work around terminal interactions.We’ve also published a short, spoiler-free guide for anyone having trouble with the opening puzzle. It points you toward where to in","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-25T18:57:13Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1847286114042729","verified_at":"2026-10-25T20:39:45Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4757720-1839676055882578","game_id":"steam-4757720","kind":"announcement","title":"THE WAKE EVENT Demo is Live!","summary":"Hey everyoneThe public demo for THE WAKE EVENT is officially available to download and play today on Steam.For context, THE WAKE EVENT is a solo-developer sci-fi mystery set aboard ARGUS Station. It’s focused entirely on exploration, reading the environment, and terminal command puzzles rather than combat or jump scares.What’s Included in the Demo:The Awakening Area: The intro habitat where you learn basic physical movement and terminal controls.Three Modules: Play through Module 01 (Wake Sequen","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-07-29T13:38:11Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1839676055882578","verified_at":"2026-10-20T17:02:13Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-4757720":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T14:06:53Z","status":"ok","all_sources_checked_at":"2026-10-26T14